The VTIMEZONE component now converts between local time and UTC on its own, without consulting the timezone database of the operating system. :meth:`Timezone.transitions_between <icalendar.cal.timezone.Timezone.transitions_between>` computes transitions from the STANDARD/DAYLIGHT sub-components and their RRULE/RDATE properties in a finite window, and the new methods ``Timezone.local_to_utc``, ``Timezone.utc_to_local``, ``Timezone.offsets_for_local`` and ``Timezone.utc_offset_at`` resolve naive local times with explicit fold (``earlier``/``later``/``reject``) and gap (``shift-forward``/``reject``) policies. Ambiguous and imaginary local times raise the new :class:`icalendar.error.AmbiguousLocalTime` and :class:`icalendar.error.NonExistentLocalTime` diagnostics, and instants not covered by the rules raise :class:`icalendar.error.InsufficientTimezoneData` instead of silently assuming UTC.
